    "result_text": "There's only one test class in the project, and it passes. \n\nThe change is complete. Here's a summary of what I implemented:\n\n## Change: derive `timezone` from locality/region\n\nThe `timezone` field is an IANA name derived at read time from the owner's region via the fixed table NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane.\n\n**Three edits**, following the existing patterns in the codebase:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `timezone` string property to the Owner schema (right after `locality`), so the OpenAPI generator produces `OwnerDto.getTimezone()/setTimezone()`.\n\n2. **`OwnerLocality.java`** \u2014 Added a `REGION_TIMEZONE` table and a `timezoneForRegion(String region)` helper that returns the IANA name (or `null` when the region is absent/unknown), mirroring the existing region-lookup helpers.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` for `timezone` that resolves the region the same way `locality` does (off the `customerCode`) and passes it through `timezoneForRegion`, keeping timezone consistent with the owner's single region-and-hash identity.\n\n**Result:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 BUILD SUCCESS. The new `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` asserts `locality=NSW` and `timezone=Australia/Sydney` for a Sydney owner, and passes.",
